1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:03,305
[Characters, places and incidents
in this production]

2
00:00:03,305 --> 00:00:06,649
[are entirely fictitious.]

3
00:00:06,649 --> 00:00:09,969
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

4
00:00:59,280 --> 00:01:00,840
<i>These are Dao's and my DNA test results.</i>

5
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:05,620
<i>She'd never be okay with it if she found out...
she was born to irresponsible parents.</i>

6
00:01:05,620 --> 00:01:07,250
<i>Have you ever had a boyfriend?</i>

7
00:01:07,250 --> 00:01:08,200
<i>I have.</i>

8
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:10,620
<i>And where is he now?</i>

9
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:12,840
<i>I'm her daughter.</i>

10
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:14,940
<i>I could reach her just now,
but she's turned off her phone.</i>

11
00:01:14,940 --> 00:01:17,680
<i>Ran still loves you. She never forgot you.</i>

12
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:19,451
<i>I want to break off our engagement.</i>

13
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:23,980
<i>So didn't you love the baby in her belly?</i>

14
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,600
<i>I'll protect my family.</i>

15
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:34,565
Well, can you act out the scene
you just mentioned as a little teaser?

16
00:01:34,565 --> 00:01:36,870
Bring in the noodles, please.

17
00:01:36,870 --> 00:01:38,710
Wow.

18
00:01:38,710 --> 00:01:40,590
- They're well-prepared, huh?
- Very.

19
00:01:41,570 --> 00:01:44,117
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

20
00:01:44,117 --> 00:01:46,248
<i>Uncle Yai, what are you doing?</i>

21
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:48,580
<i>I'm in the studio</i>

22
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:52,264
<i>watching Sam and Luknut film
a TV show together to promote the series.</i>

23
00:01:57,420 --> 00:01:58,900
I'm sorry.

24
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:02,756
<i>You can come watch
after you finish your extra class.</i>

25
00:02:05,260 --> 00:02:08,360
I want to ask for his signature!

26
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:20,340
Hello,

27
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:23,400
Auntie, I'm done with work at MJTV.

28
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:26,416
Let's meet in the condo lobby.

29
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:29,650
We'll go to an event this evening.

30
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:35,892
Do you have some spare time, Sam?

31
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:38,260
What is it?

32
00:02:39,020 --> 00:02:42,220
Someone wants to take a photo
and get your signature.

33
00:02:42,220 --> 00:02:43,345
Who?

34
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:45,720
Someone I love.

35
00:02:46,898 --> 00:02:48,306
Ms. Ran?

36
00:02:48,910 --> 00:02:51,610
- Probably not...
- Not Ran.

37
00:02:51,610 --> 00:02:52,910
Then who?

38
00:02:52,910 --> 00:02:54,400
Uncle Yai!

39
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:57,642
Oh, it's Dao.

40
00:02:58,440 --> 00:03:00,380
- Your niece?
- My daughter!

41
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:04,541
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

42
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:06,940
Daughter?

43
00:03:10,127 --> 00:03:12,780
- Younger sister?
- Daughter!

44
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:20,689
[Sam]

45
00:03:33,608 --> 00:03:35,405
Are you pulling my leg?

46
00:03:36,716 --> 00:03:39,257
Why would I joke about this?

47
00:03:39,920 --> 00:03:41,102
Yai,

48
00:03:42,810 --> 00:03:44,062
that's great!

49
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:47,350
Okay, I'll back off.

50
00:03:47,350 --> 00:03:51,580
But wait... Won't Nana throw a fit?

51
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:54,080
She didn't say anything. She was pretty quiet.

52
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:55,452
I see.

53
00:03:55,452 --> 00:03:58,016
She must've given up, then.

54
00:03:58,810 --> 00:04:01,016
Now that your daughter is this old.

55
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:04,100
She may not want to be seen...

56
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:05,766
as a husband stealer.

57
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:09,859
When will you make a public statement?

58
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:13,250
Why would I? I'm not a celebrity.

59
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:16,266
Then...

60
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:19,063
when is the wedding?

61
00:04:24,516 --> 00:04:28,010
Ran is strong-willed,
and she tends to belittle herself.

62
00:04:28,010 --> 00:04:31,883
I helped flirt with her for Uncle Yai,
and now I'm out of tricks!

63
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:34,720
Go.

64
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:37,770
It's time to go home, Mr. Rangsiman.

65
00:04:37,770 --> 00:04:39,530
Take your daughter home to your wife.

66
00:04:39,530 --> 00:04:42,710
No more working.
You can finish it later, right?

67
00:04:42,710 --> 00:04:43,710
Sam...

68
00:04:48,937 --> 00:04:50,281
Dao.

69
00:04:51,437 --> 00:04:53,990
Help your father win your mother over.

70
00:04:53,990 --> 00:04:57,560
If you can pull it off,
I'll give you ten front-row concert tickets.

71
00:04:57,560 --> 00:05:00,220
You're such a gentleman, Sam!

72
00:05:00,220 --> 00:05:02,632
- Deal?
- It's a deal!

73
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:11,179
Thanks, Sam.

74
00:05:12,223 --> 00:05:16,863
It's alright,
because I'll always be on your side.

75
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:29,040
Well, Auntie,

76
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:32,590
you don't have to come
to the event with me today.

77
00:05:32,590 --> 00:05:35,510
Actually, we don't have to
go to events together anymore.

78
00:05:37,111 --> 00:05:39,240
I'll get straight to the point.

79
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:42,340
Today is going to be your last day
working for me.

80
00:05:44,310 --> 00:05:48,580
Because... everything on my schedule
is canceled.

81
00:05:49,641 --> 00:05:53,048
I don't think I can keep hiring you anymore.

82
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:55,760
Is it because of me?

83
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:59,357
No. It's my issue,
and not your fault at all.

84
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:03,161
I think my time is up.

85
00:06:04,635 --> 00:06:07,419
I'm sorry, Auntie.

86
00:06:08,704 --> 00:06:11,021
I can compensate you.

87
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:15,970
How about this?
Would you like to go back to work at MJTV?

88
00:06:15,970 --> 00:06:20,630
I can get you a job there to work as...
Yai's secretary.

89
00:06:24,539 --> 00:06:25,986
No, thank you.

90
00:06:26,825 --> 00:06:29,680
You've helped me so much already.

91
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:31,739
Thank you so much.

92
00:06:31,739 --> 00:06:35,167
As for the compensation,
I'll have to decline it.

93
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:38,790
I respect your decision, Auntie.

94
00:06:48,154 --> 00:06:49,556
Here's your keycard.

95
00:06:50,710 --> 00:06:51,710
Yes.

96
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:01,890
Wait here for now, Dao.

97
00:07:01,890 --> 00:07:05,360
If you need anything, just tell Ms. Wan.

98
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:08,040
- Okay,
- I'll take care of some work for 15 minutes.

99
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:08,981
Okay.

100
00:07:12,060 --> 00:07:13,900
[Grandma]

101
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:15,663
Yai is here, Grandma.

102
00:07:23,582 --> 00:07:25,208
Are you working?

103
00:07:26,604 --> 00:07:27,349
Yes.

104
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:29,997
Why are you sitting at my desk?

105
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:33,264
I took over your job.

106
00:07:35,100 --> 00:07:38,220
I'm ready to take care of this for you.

107
00:07:38,940 --> 00:07:41,680
I told you so many times, but you refused.

108
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:42,890
Why now?

109
00:07:44,927 --> 00:07:48,552
Because I want my sister-in-law
and niece back.

110
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:52,540
If I let you keep being a workaholic,

111
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:55,419
Ran might have to find a new husband.

112
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:04,489
The thing you both share

113
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:08,606
is that you always
take care of others before yourselves.

114
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:14,670
It's time for you to
take care of your own heart.

115
00:08:17,010 --> 00:08:18,091
Go.

116
00:08:19,412 --> 00:08:21,395
Get your lover back.

117
00:08:26,751 --> 00:08:28,387
Thank you so much, Lek.

118
00:08:30,845 --> 00:08:32,872
It's time to leave, Yai. Go!

119
00:08:41,310 --> 00:08:42,930
You heard that, Grandma?

120
00:08:42,930 --> 00:08:45,310
Yes, thank you so much, Lek.

121
00:08:57,852 --> 00:08:59,764
I'm home, Ran.

122
00:09:02,572 --> 00:09:04,359
Thank you for driving her home.

123
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:07,860
Then I'll...

124
00:09:09,700 --> 00:09:10,800
go now.

125
00:09:11,390 --> 00:09:12,289
Yes.

126
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:15,843
Bye-bye, Uncle Yai. See you tomorrow.

127
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:39,538
I can't start my car.
Is there a car repair shop nearby?

128
00:09:39,538 --> 00:09:43,857
Yeah. But it's probably closed now.
It'll open again at 9 A.M. tomorrow.

129
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:49,607
Then stay here for the night, Uncle Yai.
You can go back tomorrow.

130
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:55,580
Did you ask Ran if she wanted me to stay here?

131
00:09:55,580 --> 00:09:58,400
If she won't let you stay,
then she's so heartless.

132
00:09:58,400 --> 00:10:01,930
Dao! Our house only has two bedrooms.

133
00:10:01,930 --> 00:10:04,700
Uncle Yai, go take a shower first.
I'll find you some clothes.

134
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:05,716
Come on.

135
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:21,290
Dao,

136
00:10:21,290 --> 00:10:23,360
what did you make your father wear?

137
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:27,521
It's Danai's pajamas.
They fit him perfectly, and they're cute, too.

138
00:10:41,903 --> 00:10:44,161
Dao, come sleep in the middle.

139
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:53,780
My dream finally came true.

140
00:10:53,780 --> 00:10:56,200
Dad's on this side and Mom's on this side.

141
00:11:02,731 --> 00:11:05,280
My dream finally came true.

142
00:11:05,280 --> 00:11:07,910
What is your dream, Uncle Yai?

143
00:11:07,910 --> 00:11:10,356
My dream is to hug my daughter and my wife.

144
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:17,880
I'll go take a shower.

145
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:42,127
Uncle Yai.

146
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:45,786
Why aren't you sleeping?

147
00:11:46,937 --> 00:11:49,627
I can't sleep. My heart is pounding.

148
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:54,185
- Can I ask you something?
- Go ahead.

149
00:11:55,610 --> 00:11:59,135
When did you and Ran have me?

150
00:12:09,700 --> 00:12:11,957
When we loved each other so much.

151
00:12:14,240 --> 00:12:16,870
One of my friends is named Sing

152
00:12:16,870 --> 00:12:20,150
because his parents had him in Singapore.

153
00:12:20,150 --> 00:12:21,995
While another friend is named Suk

154
00:12:21,995 --> 00:12:26,460
because her parents
could only meet on Fridays.

155
00:12:26,460 --> 00:12:27,640
What about me?

156
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:31,300
Is there anything besides
being a guiding light?

157
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:37,398
Go to sleep, Dao.

158
00:12:39,835 --> 00:12:42,000
Well, I can't sleep.

159
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,020
Stay still, and you'll fall asleep soon enough.

160
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:46,467
Ran,

161
00:12:47,380 --> 00:12:49,264
can I ask you for something?

162
00:12:49,930 --> 00:12:50,930
What?

163
00:12:52,252 --> 00:12:54,178
Can you hug me?

164
00:12:57,240 --> 00:13:00,482
Please? Ran, please?

165
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:08,977
Uncle Yai, come hug your daughter.

166
00:13:16,780 --> 00:13:19,405
Please don't destroy my dream.

167
00:13:22,582 --> 00:13:27,694
I want Ran and Uncle Yai
to keep hugging me like this.

168
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:35,936
Go to sleep.

169
00:13:47,175 --> 00:13:48,624
Go to sleep.

170
00:15:08,860 --> 00:15:10,358
It's not a dream.

171
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:12,515
Hey.

172
00:15:14,390 --> 00:15:15,571
Hey.

173
00:15:17,650 --> 00:15:19,100
- Hey!
- Ow!

174
00:15:21,300 --> 00:15:22,760
- Let go.
- So it's you?

175
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:24,690
I thought I was dreaming.

176
00:15:24,690 --> 00:15:25,805
Let go!

177
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:27,530
Let me go!

178
00:15:27,530 --> 00:15:31,310
No wonder your cheek smells so familiar.

179
00:15:32,361 --> 00:15:35,008
I told you to let go!

180
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:37,539
Ran...

181
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:42,562
Where is Dao? She's not here?

182
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:50,133
She was probably hot

183
00:15:51,125 --> 00:15:54,115
from her parents' warmth.

184
00:15:56,690 --> 00:15:58,227
Such a rascal.

185
00:16:14,460 --> 00:16:18,000
You lied about your car. Sneaky, huh?

186
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,278
Don't think you'll get to sleep here again.

187
00:16:33,520 --> 00:16:36,600
<i>If you let me be a singer,</i>

188
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:39,540
<i>I have a Plan B for you.</i>

189
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:40,900
<i>What's the plan?</i>

190
00:16:40,900 --> 00:16:43,800
<i>Not telling you. You have to say yes first.</i>

191
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:45,240
<i>No.</i>

192
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:46,528
<i>Oh...</i>

193
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:57,185
Oh wow!

194
00:17:07,614 --> 00:17:09,020
I...

195
00:17:09,020 --> 00:17:11,210
slept at my daughter's house.

196
00:17:11,210 --> 00:17:14,100
And her mother kicked you out?

197
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:19,940
Go, go, go, Yai. Go take a shower.

198
00:17:19,940 --> 00:17:22,690
Then come have breakfast with me. Go.

199
00:17:22,690 --> 00:17:23,690
Yes, Grandma.

200
00:17:31,080 --> 00:17:32,869
She's poor and still stuck-up?

201
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:34,864
Right?

202
00:17:37,750 --> 00:17:40,910
But a woman like her is quite rare.

203
00:17:40,910 --> 00:17:43,027
What I normally see...

204
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:46,778
When there's money, they all become compliant.

205
00:17:53,310 --> 00:17:55,950
That Daran girl is like that too, Mom.

206
00:17:55,950 --> 00:17:58,510
She wasn't faithful to Yai.

207
00:17:58,510 --> 00:18:00,860
She went around sleeping with a lot of men.

208
00:18:00,860 --> 00:18:02,340
Who told you that?

209
00:18:02,340 --> 00:18:05,520
Nana told me back then.

210
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:06,840
And you believed her?

211
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:10,340
Mom, Nana is from a noble family.

212
00:18:10,340 --> 00:18:12,127
She wouldn't lie.

213
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:15,500
But for Daran,

214
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:17,440
if she's really such a good woman,

215
00:18:17,440 --> 00:18:22,130
would she sleep around until she got pregnant
and then try to seduce Yai?

216
00:18:22,130 --> 00:18:23,380
Isn't that true?

217
00:18:23,380 --> 00:18:27,540
A noble person doesn't have to be born
into a rich family.

218
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:32,620
They only have to be virtuous,
do good deeds, and not harm others.

219
00:18:32,620 --> 00:18:36,510
What about you? Did you seek out the truth?

220
00:18:37,426 --> 00:18:39,440
Or did you only believe

221
00:18:39,440 --> 00:18:41,540
what you wanted to believe?

222
00:18:47,389 --> 00:18:48,647
Come in.

223
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:53,280
Chairman! You have to see this news.

224
00:18:53,280 --> 00:18:54,507
What news?

225
00:18:56,220 --> 00:18:58,350
<i>I apologize</i>

226
00:19:00,220 --> 00:19:03,300
<i>for talking about such a painful topic.</i>

227
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:05,600
<i>It might be difficult to say,</i>

228
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:08,600
<i>but I want to tell everyone
who's watching that</i>

229
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:10,100
<i>my fiancé</i>

230
00:19:11,720 --> 00:19:17,720
<i>hid his child and wife for a decade,
while being engaged to me,</i>

231
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:20,300
<i>without me knowing.</i>

232
00:19:20,300 --> 00:19:23,420
<i>If I hadn't seen the photos
someone took with good intentions,</i>

233
00:19:23,420 --> 00:19:27,499
<i>I wouldn't have believed that my fiancé</i>

234
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:30,577
<i>could be this cruel to me.</i>

235
00:19:34,620 --> 00:19:37,420
<i>That woman isn't a stranger either.</i>

236
00:19:40,194 --> 00:19:42,436
<i>She's my high school friend</i>

237
00:19:43,300 --> 00:19:46,070
<i>who's been jealous of me ever since,</i>

238
00:19:46,070 --> 00:19:48,350
<i>because my family is richer,</i>

239
00:19:48,350 --> 00:19:52,000
<i>I'm more beautiful, and smarter.</i>

240
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:56,400
I never thought that after a decade,

241
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:58,880
she'd come back for revenge

242
00:19:58,880 --> 00:20:02,140
<i>and still want to feel superior to me.</i>

243
00:20:02,140 --> 00:20:06,400
<i>My family has always supported her
in every way.</i>

244
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:11,139
<i>My father is furious,
while I'm shocked and deeply hurt.</i>

245
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:21,740
<i>These are the faces of that woman and child</i>

246
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:25,366
that Yai has kept hidden for a decade.

247
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:28,490
<i>I want to tell her,</i>

248
00:20:28,490 --> 00:20:32,000
<i>you've succeeded in
what you've been trying to do.</i>

249
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:34,498
You got your revenge.

250
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:39,010
<i>I want to ask her this.</i>

251
00:20:39,010 --> 00:20:41,200
Since we're both women

252
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:44,490
and she knew full well I'm engaged to Yai,

253
00:20:45,110 --> 00:20:47,660
why is she still doing this?

254
00:20:47,660 --> 00:20:50,207
Does she want to get revenge that badly?

255
00:20:51,340 --> 00:20:52,490
<i>If so,</i>

256
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:55,110
<i>she has succeeded.</i>

257
00:20:56,026 --> 00:20:58,732
<i>Thank you, everyone, for watching until now.</i>

258
00:21:00,110 --> 00:21:04,186
This will be the last time.
I won't ever talk about it again.

259
00:21:05,720 --> 00:21:07,006
<i>I'll need some time...</i>

260
00:21:08,120 --> 00:21:10,420
to recover from this.

261
00:21:11,980 --> 00:21:13,260
Thank you.

262
00:21:17,753 --> 00:21:20,150
She's making Ran look bad!

263
00:21:20,150 --> 00:21:21,190
Dao...

264
00:21:21,190 --> 00:21:24,300
Well, she's pissed.
I can be even harsher than Dao.

265
00:21:24,300 --> 00:21:25,460
Wanna hear it?

266
00:21:25,460 --> 00:21:27,019
Bullshit!

267
00:21:29,420 --> 00:21:32,464
Am I wrong? I'm pissed too.

268
00:21:34,313 --> 00:21:36,566
Did Uncle Yai hear about this?

269
00:21:39,300 --> 00:21:40,540
- Yai.
- What now?

270
00:21:40,540 --> 00:21:42,816
- Have you seen the news?
- I have.

271
00:21:49,403 --> 00:21:50,542
Yes?

272
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:54,668
The sponsors have all pulled out?

273
00:21:57,280 --> 00:21:58,807
I'll fix it.

274
00:22:00,510 --> 00:22:01,840
How are you going to fix this?

275
00:22:01,840 --> 00:22:05,650
Even if you aren't a celebrity,
you still have to make a statement.

276
00:22:05,650 --> 00:22:08,000
Ms. Nana twisted the truth.

277
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:11,720
You can't let her destroy you
and Ran like that.

278
00:22:16,780 --> 00:22:18,700
- Wan.
- Yes?

279
00:22:18,700 --> 00:22:21,820
Set up a room for the press conference.

280
00:22:21,820 --> 00:22:23,118
Yes.

281
00:22:29,080 --> 00:22:31,800
Is she trying to bankrupt our company?

282
00:22:31,800 --> 00:22:33,923
Isn't this going too far?

283
00:22:40,040 --> 00:22:43,790
Have you seen the temper
of the woman you think is right for Yai?

284
00:22:44,820 --> 00:22:47,740
Between a woman who's ready
to destroy everything

285
00:22:47,740 --> 00:22:49,900
without caring
if she causes trouble for others,

286
00:22:49,900 --> 00:22:52,260
just to protect her own pride,

287
00:22:53,380 --> 00:22:56,985
and a woman who sacrifices her future

288
00:22:56,985 --> 00:22:58,853
for the people she loves,

289
00:22:59,790 --> 00:23:05,415
which woman's heart
deserves to be praised more?

290
00:23:07,820 --> 00:23:09,820
You're in pain

291
00:23:09,820 --> 00:23:12,014
because I didn't accept you.

292
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:16,360
Do you understand how Yai and Daran feel?

293
00:23:17,034 --> 00:23:18,649
They were also in pain

294
00:23:19,290 --> 00:23:21,759
because you never accepted their love.

295
00:23:22,830 --> 00:23:26,056
They've spent a decade proving

296
00:23:26,880 --> 00:23:29,228
that their love is real,

297
00:23:30,161 --> 00:23:32,281
not superficial,

298
00:23:33,469 --> 00:23:35,979
and unconditional.

299
00:23:36,660 --> 00:23:39,610
All they ask is to be by each other's side.

300
00:23:48,620 --> 00:23:50,080
It's time...

301
00:23:50,910 --> 00:23:54,980
for you to correct your own mistakes.

302
00:23:56,040 --> 00:23:57,510
I admire...

303
00:23:58,610 --> 00:24:01,100
those who correct their mistakes

304
00:24:01,760 --> 00:24:03,681
not those who make excuses.

305
00:24:11,210 --> 00:24:16,246
Ms. Natasha,
all the sponsors have pulled out of MJTV.

306
00:24:22,737 --> 00:24:25,752
How are you gonna
talk your way out of it now, Yai?

307
00:24:39,630 --> 00:24:41,720
<i>Uncle Yai, I'm so angry!</i>

308
00:24:41,720 --> 00:24:44,330
<i>No need to be angry. The truth will prevail.</i>

309
00:24:44,330 --> 00:24:47,420
<i>Switch to my channel and wait for me.
I'm going all out.</i>

310
00:24:57,220 --> 00:25:00,420
[MJTV Broadcasting]

311
00:25:00,420 --> 00:25:02,970
<i>I won't be taking too much of your time.</i>

312
00:25:02,970 --> 00:25:05,190
<i>I'm here to make a statement
from my perspective,</i>

313
00:25:05,190 --> 00:25:07,520
<i>as you all have seen in Ms. Natasha's video.</i>

314
00:25:07,520 --> 00:25:11,260
Is it true that you became engaged
to Ms. Natasha,

315
00:25:11,260 --> 00:25:13,090
even though you have a family of your own?

316
00:25:13,090 --> 00:25:14,203
It's true.

317
00:25:15,430 --> 00:25:18,620
Then does that mean you're having an affair?

318
00:25:18,620 --> 00:25:20,500
There is only one person I love.

319
00:25:20,500 --> 00:25:23,970
She's my first and only love,

320
00:25:23,970 --> 00:25:25,650
the one I built my world with.

321
00:25:25,650 --> 00:25:28,273
<i>That person is
the mother of my child, Ms. Daran.</i>

322
00:25:30,220 --> 00:25:32,069
The truth will prevail...

323
00:25:33,060 --> 00:25:35,470
But the truth is, I was lied to.

324
00:25:36,100 --> 00:25:38,257
Whatever excuse you come up
with won't save you.

325
00:25:43,500 --> 00:25:45,274
<i>We loved each other so much.</i>

326
00:25:45,860 --> 00:25:48,187
<i>Daran was pregnant
when we graduated high school.</i>

327
00:25:48,940 --> 00:25:51,620
<i>Many people might think
we were too young to be parents,</i>

328
00:25:51,620 --> 00:25:53,500
<i>but we decided to keep our child.</i>

329
00:25:53,500 --> 00:25:55,038
Daran loved me so much.

330
00:25:56,950 --> 00:25:59,499
She didn't want me to give up
my future and education,

331
00:26:00,660 --> 00:26:02,710
so she broke up with me

332
00:26:02,710 --> 00:26:05,200
and lied to me, saying that our child had died,

333
00:26:05,200 --> 00:26:06,999
so that I could move on from her.

334
00:26:07,990 --> 00:26:10,160
<i>She had to become a single mother,</i>

335
00:26:10,160 --> 00:26:13,390
<i>sacrificing her own future to provide
for her child,</i>

336
00:26:13,390 --> 00:26:15,620
<i>her mother, and her brother all by herself.</i>

337
00:26:15,620 --> 00:26:17,420
I never knew...

338
00:26:18,750 --> 00:26:21,500
how much pain did
this little woman have to bear?

339
00:26:22,280 --> 00:26:23,767
<i>I'm sorry, Ran.</i>

340
00:26:24,600 --> 00:26:27,140
<i>You suffered so much because of me.</i>

341
00:26:32,110 --> 00:26:36,600
<i>I admit that I walked out of
her life full of anger.</i>

342
00:26:37,420 --> 00:26:39,060
<i>I hated her,</i>

343
00:26:39,060 --> 00:26:42,300
but I couldn't help reading the sports news.

344
00:26:42,300 --> 00:26:44,730
I still wanted to know about her.

345
00:26:46,100 --> 00:26:49,027
I wanted to see her become a national athlete,

346
00:26:50,898 --> 00:26:52,644
but I never did.

347
00:26:54,180 --> 00:26:58,550
<i>I didn't even have the courage to
find out the truth on my own until recently.</i>

348
00:27:00,326 --> 00:27:01,870
I'm sorry, Ran.

349
00:27:02,731 --> 00:27:05,363
Your life has been
full of hardships because of me.

350
00:27:09,980 --> 00:27:13,120
But you're engaged to Ms. Natasha,
even though you don't love her,

351
00:27:13,120 --> 00:27:15,180
and your heart belongs to someone else.

352
00:27:15,180 --> 00:27:18,660
Isn't this unfair to Ms. Natasha as well?

353
00:27:22,269 --> 00:27:23,987
It's my fault.

354
00:27:33,643 --> 00:27:35,307
I'm the one to blame.

355
00:27:35,994 --> 00:27:38,691
Back then, I was a mother
who made decisions for her son.

356
00:27:39,600 --> 00:27:41,433
All I thought about was that

357
00:27:42,520 --> 00:27:48,509
my son's partner had to
be of the same social status.

358
00:27:49,520 --> 00:27:51,214
I couldn't accept it

359
00:27:51,820 --> 00:27:54,940
if his partner were an ordinary woman

360
00:27:54,940 --> 00:27:56,643
with nothing to her name.

361
00:27:57,420 --> 00:27:59,420
<i>I threatened Daran...</i>

362
00:28:00,280 --> 00:28:02,034
<i>to break up with Rangsiman.</i>

363
00:28:04,120 --> 00:28:05,368
If she didn't,

364
00:28:06,180 --> 00:28:09,472
I'd make sure neither of them
had a place in society.

365
00:28:10,760 --> 00:28:13,511
And I even forced...

366
00:28:15,019 --> 00:28:16,472
Daran...

367
00:28:17,900 --> 00:28:19,540
to have an abortion.

368
00:28:19,540 --> 00:28:21,081
- Oh.
- Abortion?

369
00:28:21,960 --> 00:28:23,340
That's so cruel.

370
00:28:24,480 --> 00:28:26,854
I also forced my son...

371
00:28:28,600 --> 00:28:30,460
to get engaged to Natasha.

372
00:28:30,460 --> 00:28:35,790
<i>I hid the fact that
Daran was pregnant from Natasha</i>

373
00:28:35,790 --> 00:28:41,237
because I wanted my son to have a clean slate.

374
00:28:46,138 --> 00:28:51,636
Rangsiman loves his mother
and is very grateful to her.

375
00:28:52,700 --> 00:28:54,800
He was in pain,

376
00:28:55,617 --> 00:28:57,995
yet he did everything I ordered him to do.

377
00:29:03,930 --> 00:29:05,839
Everyone was hurt

378
00:29:08,220 --> 00:29:09,554
because of me.

379
00:29:15,020 --> 00:29:16,222
Yai,

380
00:29:17,920 --> 00:29:21,675
I'm sorry for everything that happened.

381
00:29:23,910 --> 00:29:24,964
Today...

382
00:29:25,890 --> 00:29:28,893
let me do something for you for once.

383
00:29:30,520 --> 00:29:36,130
If society wants someone to blame,
can you let me take the blame, Yai?

384
00:29:37,490 --> 00:29:38,542
Mom...

385
00:29:52,360 --> 00:29:54,507
I apologize to everyone.

386
00:29:55,100 --> 00:29:57,210
None of what happened

387
00:29:57,210 --> 00:29:59,542
was my son's fault at all.

388
00:30:00,310 --> 00:30:04,003
It's all because of me. It's all because of me.

389
00:30:10,260 --> 00:30:14,557
Perhaps she got hit by Grandma's spell.
She suddenly changed.

390
00:30:20,350 --> 00:30:22,220
- Mom!
- Mom!

391
00:30:22,220 --> 00:30:24,030
Aoyjai!

392
00:30:24,030 --> 00:30:25,151
Who?

393
00:30:26,220 --> 00:30:28,460
She's my childhood friend.

394
00:30:28,460 --> 00:30:30,240
We grew up in the market together.

395
00:30:30,240 --> 00:30:32,700
Her stall was next to mine!

396
00:30:32,700 --> 00:30:34,640
But her name is Angkhana.

397
00:30:34,640 --> 00:30:37,400
Yai said she won several beauty pageants.

398
00:30:37,400 --> 00:30:40,390
If that's the case, then it must be her!

399
00:30:40,390 --> 00:30:42,720
When she was younger,
she wanted to enter beauty pageants.

400
00:30:42,720 --> 00:30:44,100
Then it's the same person.

401
00:30:44,100 --> 00:30:45,330
As a teenager,

402
00:30:45,330 --> 00:30:47,780
I heard she ran away
from home and disappeared.

403
00:30:47,780 --> 00:30:51,620
That means she changed her name
to reinvent herself.

404
00:30:51,620 --> 00:30:55,080
What? Grandma Aoyjai.

405
00:30:55,080 --> 00:30:59,090
She said we're low-class kids,
but she's no different from us.

406
00:30:59,090 --> 00:31:02,011
Dao, don't talk about your grandma like that.

407
00:31:03,600 --> 00:31:08,620
Dao, Aoyjai probably came to her senses.
That's why she said all of that.

408
00:31:08,620 --> 00:31:10,480
Sadhu!

409
00:31:14,745 --> 00:31:18,220
Hello, I'm Mr. Rangsiman's brother,

410
00:31:18,220 --> 00:31:21,910
who went to the same school
as Ms. Natasha and Ms. Daran.

411
00:31:21,910 --> 00:31:26,709
I guarantee you that the truth
between Ms. Natasha and Ms. Daran...

412
00:31:27,400 --> 00:31:30,866
is completely different
from what you've been told.

413
00:31:33,280 --> 00:31:35,839
The jealous one was Ms. Natasha.

414
00:31:36,960 --> 00:31:39,784
She envied her studies and Mr. Rangsiman.

415
00:31:40,640 --> 00:31:42,920
<i>She tried to pick on Ms. Daran.</i>

416
00:31:42,920 --> 00:31:45,600
<i>She even put a piece of
glass in Ms. Daran's shoe,</i>

417
00:31:45,600 --> 00:31:47,620
causing her an injury.

418
00:31:47,620 --> 00:31:51,980
I heard with my own ears
that it was Ms. Natasha and her friends.

419
00:31:51,980 --> 00:31:53,790
Ms. Daran...

420
00:31:53,790 --> 00:31:58,250
knew who did it, but she chose
not to take action against anyone.

421
00:31:58,250 --> 00:32:00,304
So I took matters into my own hands.

422
00:32:00,304 --> 00:32:02,610
You can ask Ms. Natasha

423
00:32:02,610 --> 00:32:04,580
<i>about the cockroaches in the bathroom.</i>

424
00:32:04,580 --> 00:32:06,510
So it was you?

425
00:32:06,510 --> 00:32:08,140
Lek!

426
00:32:08,140 --> 00:32:09,615
You little shit!

427
00:32:11,530 --> 00:32:13,390
Can I have a brief moment?

428
00:32:13,390 --> 00:32:14,680
I won't take long.

429
00:32:14,680 --> 00:32:19,210
There's one more thing
I would like to inform everyone.

430
00:32:19,210 --> 00:32:25,040
All TV shows and series
produced by Sahaphet are now void

431
00:32:25,040 --> 00:32:27,860
because Sahaphet breached the contract.

432
00:32:27,860 --> 00:32:31,720
But our company won't be
asking for any compensation.

433
00:32:31,720 --> 00:32:34,160
Consider it compensation
for the sudden termination.

434
00:32:34,160 --> 00:32:36,560
And MJTV...

435
00:32:36,560 --> 00:32:40,040
will buy back all the shares
that Sahaphet bought.

436
00:32:40,040 --> 00:32:42,350
I hope we can reach an agreement on good terms.

437
00:32:43,900 --> 00:32:46,151
Thank you so much, everyone.

438
00:32:49,452 --> 00:32:53,233
Mr. Rangsiman! So Sahaphet can't
remain a shareholder anymore, right?

439
00:33:00,360 --> 00:33:02,780
Uncle Yai is so cool, right, Ran?

440
00:33:15,440 --> 00:33:16,740
Nana!

441
00:33:16,740 --> 00:33:19,249
The stocks! Our company's stocks are falling!

442
00:33:23,060 --> 00:33:24,248
Nana!

443
00:33:24,840 --> 00:33:25,820
Nana!

444
00:33:27,100 --> 00:33:30,400
I can see that!
I told you to call me "Miss", didn't I?

445
00:33:30,400 --> 00:33:34,522
Why don't you understand?
Idiot! You're a fucking idiot!

446
00:33:36,670 --> 00:33:38,014
You're the idiot!

447
00:33:39,650 --> 00:33:41,200
You don't think before you act.

448
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:44,375
Don't you see that what you did
almost made your company go bankrupt?

449
00:33:44,375 --> 00:33:47,340
And you're still being arrogant,
ordering everyone around.

450
00:33:47,340 --> 00:33:49,690
Even though you see me
as dirt beneath your feet,

451
00:33:49,690 --> 00:33:52,370
I'm still human.
I have a mom and dad just like you!

452
00:33:52,370 --> 00:33:54,600
I have my limits, too!

453
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:57,700
The only good thing
about working with you is the money.

454
00:33:57,700 --> 00:34:00,850
Other than that, there's nothing!
I'm fucking done.

455
00:34:00,850 --> 00:34:03,830
Get out! Get the fuck out of my company!

456
00:34:03,830 --> 00:34:06,380
Fine! I don't care.

457
00:34:06,380 --> 00:34:10,733
If you're going to keep acting like this,
then be alone until you die!

458
00:34:12,740 --> 00:34:15,240
Oh, let me tell you something.

459
00:34:15,240 --> 00:34:18,500
Yai actually made the right choice,

460
00:34:18,500 --> 00:34:21,327
because he's not stupid. Serves you right.

461
00:34:23,530 --> 00:34:24,800
Get out!

462
00:34:24,800 --> 00:34:27,510
I hope your life is miserable,
I hope your life is shit!

463
00:34:27,510 --> 00:34:29,616
Go to hell!

464
00:34:55,680 --> 00:34:58,240
Mom, thank you so much

465
00:34:58,240 --> 00:35:00,434
for changing for me.

466
00:35:03,631 --> 00:35:05,933
A mother's greatest wish

467
00:35:06,581 --> 00:35:08,965
is for her child to be happy.

468
00:35:10,913 --> 00:35:13,503
Will you forgive me, Yai?

469
00:35:21,310 --> 00:35:22,310
I...

470
00:35:24,454 --> 00:35:29,160
I never did anything to make you proud of me.

471
00:35:29,160 --> 00:35:30,934
From now on,

472
00:35:32,582 --> 00:35:35,575
I'll do anything for you.

473
00:35:36,520 --> 00:35:37,723
Is that okay?

474
00:35:57,810 --> 00:35:59,369
Thank you.

475
00:36:01,100 --> 00:36:03,810
Do you remember me, Aoyjai?

476
00:36:06,010 --> 00:36:08,060
Oh! Oh no.

477
00:36:08,760 --> 00:36:12,160
Here, have some tissues. Wipe your mouth.

478
00:36:18,140 --> 00:36:21,856
It's me, Dueanchan, from the municipal market.

479
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:26,100
Dueanchan? Wait.

480
00:36:27,200 --> 00:36:29,333
You're Daran's mother?

481
00:36:30,580 --> 00:36:32,273
It's a small world.

482
00:36:33,100 --> 00:36:37,900
Mommy Duean said your name is Aoyjai... right?

483
00:36:37,900 --> 00:36:39,700
That's my old name.

484
00:36:39,700 --> 00:36:43,000
Just forget about it.
I have changed my name now.

485
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:47,240
Then, what is Grandma Aoyjai doing here?

486
00:36:47,240 --> 00:36:49,700
If you're here to pick a fight
with my family...

487
00:36:49,700 --> 00:36:51,723
I came to apologize to everyone.

488
00:36:57,563 --> 00:37:00,173
Especially you, Daran.

489
00:37:02,910 --> 00:37:04,854
Will you forgive me?

490
00:37:06,280 --> 00:37:08,876
I truly wronged you,

491
00:37:09,640 --> 00:37:11,893
and now it's eating at me.

492
00:37:13,925 --> 00:37:16,283
I never felt happy

493
00:37:19,127 --> 00:37:21,682
ever since I took Yai away from you.

494
00:37:23,429 --> 00:37:25,578
I understand you well.

495
00:37:30,841 --> 00:37:33,126
You can call me Mother.

496
00:37:40,300 --> 00:37:41,710
Yes,

497
00:37:41,710 --> 00:37:43,010
Mother.

498
00:37:46,145 --> 00:37:49,000
Now that you called me Mother,

499
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:52,369
that makes you... my daughter-in-law.

500
00:37:54,180 --> 00:37:56,329
You'll have to marry Yai.

501
00:37:59,565 --> 00:38:02,350
I'm not marrying him, Mrs. Angkhana.

502
00:38:02,350 --> 00:38:03,615
- What?
- What?

503
00:38:19,365 --> 00:38:21,500
I couldn't convince her.

504
00:38:21,500 --> 00:38:24,400
I don't know if there's anything
that hasn't been resolved yet.

505
00:38:24,400 --> 00:38:26,660
You did very well today.

506
00:38:26,660 --> 00:38:28,615
I commend you.

507
00:38:29,940 --> 00:38:32,600
Thank you, Mom.

508
00:38:32,600 --> 00:38:35,000
Do you love me more now?

509
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:36,310
No.

510
00:38:37,640 --> 00:38:38,662
Yai,

511
00:38:39,480 --> 00:38:42,040
you have to be the one to do this.

512
00:38:42,040 --> 00:38:43,810
Because everyone already...

513
00:38:43,810 --> 00:38:45,850
helped as much as they could.

514
00:38:51,849 --> 00:38:54,083
You can't sleep here tonight.

515
00:38:55,320 --> 00:38:56,522
I'm not.

516
00:38:57,980 --> 00:38:59,663
I just want to ask

517
00:39:00,598 --> 00:39:02,678
why you're still being cold with me

518
00:39:04,003 --> 00:39:06,615
when everything has already been resolved?

519
00:39:08,555 --> 00:39:10,154
What do I have to do, Ran?

520
00:39:11,840 --> 00:39:14,006
For you to give me a chance to...

521
00:39:15,980 --> 00:39:17,522
be your husband,

522
00:39:18,510 --> 00:39:19,842
be our child's father,

523
00:39:21,220 --> 00:39:23,506
and be part of your family once more?

524
00:39:26,468 --> 00:39:27,615
I know...

525
00:39:29,849 --> 00:39:31,490
that you still love me.

526
00:39:34,630 --> 00:39:36,154
Then why, Ran?

527
00:39:38,100 --> 00:39:39,325
Why?

528
00:39:41,460 --> 00:39:43,540
Uncle Yai! Uncle Yai, look!

529
00:39:43,540 --> 00:39:45,790
Ran still has her taekwondo uniform.

530
00:39:45,790 --> 00:39:48,000
If you're not practicing anymore,
can I have it?

531
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:51,380
I want to be good at it, and maybe
I can make your dream come true.

532
00:39:59,379 --> 00:40:00,579
Ran!

533
00:40:09,253 --> 00:40:12,264
Did I say something that upset Ran?

534
00:40:14,210 --> 00:40:16,140
Ran is grieving for her father.

535
00:40:16,140 --> 00:40:18,400
She never wore it or practiced taekwondo again.

536
00:40:18,400 --> 00:40:21,201
She probably went to cry alone again.

537
00:40:23,174 --> 00:40:24,787
I shouldn't have said that.

538
00:40:25,420 --> 00:40:27,720
Oh, it's okay, dear.

539
00:40:27,720 --> 00:40:30,270
You can talk to us and ask questions
so we can tell you.

540
00:40:30,270 --> 00:40:32,787
We'll have no secrets, alright?

541
00:40:34,060 --> 00:40:35,419
What happened?

542
00:40:36,260 --> 00:40:38,455
Ran has some issues regarding her father.

543
00:40:42,850 --> 00:40:44,024
[2026]

544
00:40:44,910 --> 00:40:45,930
[2013]

545
00:40:45,930 --> 00:40:47,907
<i>Hello? Dear...</i>

546
00:40:49,160 --> 00:40:53,305
<i>can you help calm Ran down?
I feel so bad for her.</i>

547
00:40:53,305 --> 00:40:54,442
<i>Please?</i>

548
00:40:55,940 --> 00:40:59,350
<i>Ran, your father wants to talk to you.</i>

549
00:41:14,820 --> 00:41:15,895
<i>Dad...</i>

550
00:41:16,940 --> 00:41:19,793
<i>It's okay. It's okay. It's okay.</i>

551
00:41:20,760 --> 00:41:22,907
<i>Yai left me.</i>

552
00:41:26,070 --> 00:41:31,050
<i>I'm sorry... I destroyed your dream.</i>

553
00:41:32,917 --> 00:41:35,800
<i>It's alright, Ran. It's okay.</i>

554
00:41:35,800 --> 00:41:40,160
<i>Listen, Ran, I can raise a grandchild</i>

555
00:41:40,160 --> 00:41:43,700
<i>and I'll raise them to be
as cute as you are, okay?</i>

556
00:41:46,000 --> 00:41:49,100
<i>Listen to me, Ran, it's okay.</i>

557
00:41:49,100 --> 00:41:51,340
<i>I'm okay. You don't have to cry.</i>

558
00:41:52,400 --> 00:41:54,110
<i>I'll...</i>

559
00:41:54,110 --> 00:41:57,170
<i>I'll change my ticket so I can go back tonight.</i>

560
00:41:57,170 --> 00:42:00,777
<i>So don't cry. I'm coming back to you, okay?</i>

561
00:42:02,494 --> 00:42:04,605
<i>I'll wait for you.</i>

562
00:42:11,300 --> 00:42:12,980
<i>Mom...</i>

563
00:42:12,980 --> 00:42:16,760
<i>It's okay... It's okay, Ran...</i>

564
00:42:16,760 --> 00:42:18,740
<i>I'm here.</i>

565
00:42:34,089 --> 00:42:35,680
<i>Mom...</i>

566
00:42:35,680 --> 00:42:37,386
<i>When will Dad get here?</i>

567
00:42:49,810 --> 00:42:51,104
<i>Hello.</i>

568
00:43:01,777 --> 00:43:06,240
<i>The bus your father took last night
flipped over in Ayutthaya.</i>

569
00:43:06,240 --> 00:43:09,167
<i>What about Dad? Where is he?</i>

570
00:43:09,920 --> 00:43:13,900
<i>They said... Dad passed away!</i>

571
00:43:16,090 --> 00:43:20,000
<i>No! Dad said he'd come back to me!</i>

572
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:21,910
<i>So he has to come back!</i>

573
00:43:21,910 --> 00:43:23,548
<i>Mom!</i>

574
00:43:25,360 --> 00:43:26,440
<i>- Ran...
- Mom...</i>

575
00:43:26,440 --> 00:43:29,200
<i>Mom, Mom... It's not true.</i>

576
00:43:29,200 --> 00:43:31,390
<i>I'm going to find Dad...</i>

577
00:43:31,390 --> 00:43:34,810
<i>- Dad...
- Ran! Ran! Ran!</i>

578
00:43:34,810 --> 00:43:37,272
<i>I'm going to find Dad!</i>

579
00:43:41,820 --> 00:43:43,486
<i>Ran, dear.</i>

580
00:43:46,740 --> 00:43:49,149
<i>It's my fault he died.</i>

581
00:43:50,248 --> 00:43:51,310
<i>Don't think like that.</i>

582
00:43:51,310 --> 00:43:55,030
<i>- It's my fault!
- Ran, Ran...</i>

583
00:44:02,430 --> 00:44:05,160
After her father's funeral,

584
00:44:05,160 --> 00:44:07,320
Ran came up to me and said

585
00:44:07,320 --> 00:44:10,375
she'll take care of everything in Dad's place.

586
00:44:11,650 --> 00:44:12,930
After that,

587
00:44:13,520 --> 00:44:16,220
I never saw her happy

588
00:44:16,220 --> 00:44:18,985
or passionate about her dreams ever again.

589
00:44:18,985 --> 00:44:22,742
It's like she's always punishing herself.

590
00:44:27,165 --> 00:44:28,965
Ran is so mean...

591
00:44:29,630 --> 00:44:31,910
She's so mean to herself.

592
00:44:35,950 --> 00:44:39,290
Uncle Yai, you have to help her.

593
00:45:27,200 --> 00:45:28,200
Ran,

594
00:45:29,220 --> 00:45:30,812
I'm here.

595
00:45:36,900 --> 00:45:37,806
You...

596
00:45:44,100 --> 00:45:46,210
I learned about your father.

597
00:45:49,180 --> 00:45:51,040
Did Mom tell you that?

598
00:45:51,040 --> 00:45:52,481
Ran, listen to me.

599
00:45:53,410 --> 00:45:54,910
It was an accident.

600
00:45:55,720 --> 00:45:59,262
No one died because of anyone else. Ran...

601
00:46:01,900 --> 00:46:05,582
If you think what happened
to your father was your fault,

602
00:46:07,490 --> 00:46:09,934
then it's my fault as well.

603
00:46:11,510 --> 00:46:13,918
Should I punish myself like you do?

604
00:46:29,920 --> 00:46:31,981
I'm not going to the TV station today.

605
00:46:32,820 --> 00:46:35,200
Do as you please. Make your own choices.

606
00:46:36,448 --> 00:46:39,153
And if the commercial still doesn't sell,
then leave it.

607
00:46:39,900 --> 00:46:41,887
Maybe you can cancel the show later.

608
00:46:42,860 --> 00:46:45,394
We can just keep the screen black.

609
00:46:46,450 --> 00:46:50,120
You... This will
cause trouble for everyone else.

610
00:46:50,120 --> 00:46:53,250
You worry about everyone else,
but why not yourself, Ran?

611
00:46:53,250 --> 00:46:54,640
Answer me.

612
00:46:55,520 --> 00:46:58,100
This happened because of the two of us,

613
00:46:58,100 --> 00:47:01,898
so why do you have to be the one
carrying all this guilt?

614
00:47:08,888 --> 00:47:10,973
Can you tell me...

615
00:47:11,820 --> 00:47:13,638
what I should do?

616
00:47:15,220 --> 00:47:17,850
Should we go back in time?

617
00:47:17,850 --> 00:47:19,981
Go back and fix everything.

618
00:47:21,200 --> 00:47:24,720
So that we never meet, never fall in love,

619
00:47:24,720 --> 00:47:27,000
and never have Dao.

620
00:47:27,000 --> 00:47:28,720
Does that sound good, Ran?

621
00:47:28,720 --> 00:47:30,949
It's impossible, and you know that.

622
00:47:31,600 --> 00:47:34,120
And don't say "never have Dao."

623
00:47:34,120 --> 00:47:35,742
I can't take it.

624
00:47:36,440 --> 00:47:38,542
If it's impossible,

625
00:47:39,810 --> 00:47:42,190
then why are you doing this?

626
00:47:42,190 --> 00:47:43,880
Think about it.

627
00:47:44,690 --> 00:47:46,583
Would your father be happy

628
00:47:48,480 --> 00:47:51,280
if he saw the daughter he loved,

629
00:47:51,280 --> 00:47:53,404
the girl who used to be cheerful,

630
00:47:54,640 --> 00:47:56,700
full of energy,

631
00:47:56,700 --> 00:47:58,610
and ambitious,

632
00:47:58,610 --> 00:48:02,169
ended up burying herself in guilt like this?

633
00:48:04,235 --> 00:48:07,364
But some emotions are hard to get rid of.

634
00:48:11,490 --> 00:48:14,177
Have you ever tried it?

635
00:48:15,240 --> 00:48:17,400
Can't we start again?

636
00:48:17,400 --> 00:48:20,410
Why don't you let go of all the bad memories

637
00:48:20,410 --> 00:48:22,817
and hold on to the good ones?

638
00:48:23,960 --> 00:48:27,240
If you think Daddy Sak
passed away because of you,

639
00:48:27,240 --> 00:48:28,800
I can't help but think.

640
00:48:28,800 --> 00:48:30,960
Without me,

641
00:48:30,960 --> 00:48:33,460
things might not have gotten this complicated.

642
00:48:33,460 --> 00:48:35,400
Dao...

643
00:48:35,400 --> 00:48:38,200
It has nothing to do with you.
It isn't your fault.

644
00:48:38,200 --> 00:48:42,330
Well, if you still blame yourself,

645
00:48:42,330 --> 00:48:43,927
I'll do it as well.

646
00:48:44,800 --> 00:48:46,009
Ran,

647
00:48:48,200 --> 00:48:51,615
I'm not asking you to
go back to your old self...

648
00:48:53,100 --> 00:48:55,390
I know it's hard.

649
00:48:55,390 --> 00:48:57,896
And I never wanted to push you.

650
00:48:58,710 --> 00:49:02,140
I just want you to let your walls down,

651
00:49:03,110 --> 00:49:05,974
so others can help you.

652
00:49:08,765 --> 00:49:11,230
We can slowly heal, one step at a time, Ran.

653
00:49:11,230 --> 00:49:12,320
Did you know that?

654
00:49:13,180 --> 00:49:14,590
Yes,

655
00:49:14,590 --> 00:49:16,400
I'm going to take good care of you.

656
00:49:16,400 --> 00:49:19,104
I'll water you, tend the soil,
and give you fertilizer every day.

657
00:49:20,120 --> 00:49:22,865
Your heart will definitely heal that way.

658
00:49:34,350 --> 00:49:36,550
Even if Daddy Sak isn't here anymore,

659
00:49:37,500 --> 00:49:39,636
I'm still here, Ran.

660
00:49:40,660 --> 00:49:43,900
We should support each other.

661
00:49:47,460 --> 00:49:51,600
You should hold on to
what's good for your heart, alright?

662
00:50:42,110 --> 00:50:43,529
Heartbroken?

663
00:50:44,620 --> 00:50:45,763
Why?

664
00:50:47,801 --> 00:50:50,466
Are you here to laugh at me or something?

665
00:50:51,723 --> 00:50:53,620
Just give up.

666
00:50:53,620 --> 00:50:56,020
Even I was able to move on.

667
00:50:56,020 --> 00:50:57,849
Why do you have to hold onto it?

668
00:50:59,900 --> 00:51:02,200
How could someone like you...

669
00:51:02,200 --> 00:51:03,800
understand?

670
00:51:05,090 --> 00:51:07,580
You moved on in a month.

671
00:51:07,580 --> 00:51:10,325
Just a month,
and you already found someone else.

672
00:51:13,810 --> 00:51:16,996
It's understandable.
You've felt this way for 15 years.

673
00:51:18,702 --> 00:51:21,700
How much longer will you suffer?

674
00:51:21,700 --> 00:51:23,472
It's a waste of time.

675
00:51:26,120 --> 00:51:27,222
Hey.

676
00:51:28,510 --> 00:51:30,190
Let me ask you something.

677
00:51:31,040 --> 00:51:32,761
Aren't you tired?

678
00:51:33,750 --> 00:51:36,058
You've always followed Yai around.

679
00:51:38,510 --> 00:51:40,100
Watching you,

680
00:51:40,700 --> 00:51:42,628
I feel tired for you.

681
00:51:48,000 --> 00:51:50,238
If you were still a player in the game,

682
00:51:51,100 --> 00:51:53,535
I wouldn't be talking to you like this.

683
00:51:54,402 --> 00:51:56,448
But from what I've seen...

684
00:51:57,940 --> 00:51:59,862
You were never a player.

685
00:52:01,680 --> 00:52:03,542
You did compete,

686
00:52:04,924 --> 00:52:07,980
but you were never in Yai's eyes.

687
00:52:13,563 --> 00:52:15,948
My harsh words might be too much for you,

688
00:52:16,810 --> 00:52:18,620
but I mean well.

689
00:52:19,300 --> 00:52:24,161
Getting hurt once is better
than drowning in sorrow, yeah?

690
00:52:29,820 --> 00:52:32,288
But I didn't want to lose to her.

691
00:52:33,940 --> 00:52:37,047
I don't want to lose to anyone,
you understand me?

692
00:52:38,340 --> 00:52:39,747
This story...

693
00:52:40,370 --> 00:52:42,664
doesn't have a winner or a loser.

694
00:52:43,551 --> 00:52:45,971
You either love someone or you don't.

695
00:52:46,884 --> 00:52:48,577
But those two...

696
00:52:49,169 --> 00:52:51,900
are bound by their hearts.

697
00:52:51,900 --> 00:52:53,633
No one can separate them.

698
00:52:56,200 --> 00:52:57,578
Ms. Nana,

699
00:52:58,840 --> 00:53:00,742
listen to me.

700
00:53:04,000 --> 00:53:05,920
Just let it go.

701
00:53:13,910 --> 00:53:15,030
It's okay.

702
00:53:15,030 --> 00:53:18,410
Can you stop saying that? I'm going to cry.

703
00:53:19,480 --> 00:53:21,590
You did your best, Ms. Nana.

704
00:53:35,127 --> 00:53:36,497
Wow!

705
00:53:37,440 --> 00:53:39,003
So pretty.

706
00:53:39,980 --> 00:53:42,150
Your mother has been here before.

707
00:53:42,150 --> 00:53:44,090
Dao was born here, too.

708
00:53:44,090 --> 00:53:46,450
Yai.

709
00:53:47,720 --> 00:53:51,100
Then can I go have a look inside?

710
00:53:51,100 --> 00:53:52,370
Yeah.

711
00:53:53,060 --> 00:53:55,073
Everything here is still the same.

712
00:53:55,920 --> 00:53:57,722
You still remember it, right?

713
00:54:01,300 --> 00:54:03,238
You've struggled so much

714
00:54:04,260 --> 00:54:05,960
all this time.

715
00:54:08,800 --> 00:54:10,183
It's a shame.

716
00:54:11,086 --> 00:54:13,369
I wasn't there for you then.

717
00:54:15,980 --> 00:54:20,175
You're so strong, you know?
Getting through all of that.

718
00:54:25,453 --> 00:54:26,722
Yai...

719
00:54:27,460 --> 00:54:28,570
Yes?

720
00:54:30,176 --> 00:54:31,786
I'm sorry.

721
00:54:35,240 --> 00:54:37,756
I'm sorry for being so mean to you.

722
00:54:38,860 --> 00:54:41,300
You don't have to apologize.

723
00:54:41,300 --> 00:54:43,214
It's not your fault.

724
00:54:45,791 --> 00:54:47,620
If there's anyone to blame,

725
00:54:48,940 --> 00:54:50,355
it's me.

726
00:54:56,100 --> 00:54:58,777
Have you been doing well?

727
00:55:00,297 --> 00:55:01,785
I'm doing well.

728
00:55:02,540 --> 00:55:03,724
I ate well,

729
00:55:04,440 --> 00:55:07,175
slept well, everything is good.

730
00:55:10,966 --> 00:55:12,619
You're worried about me?

731
00:55:15,900 --> 00:55:17,775
You still love me, right?

732
00:55:21,876 --> 00:55:23,771
I want you to say it.

733
00:55:24,400 --> 00:55:25,582
I want to hear it.

734
00:55:29,980 --> 00:55:31,087
I...

735
00:55:37,170 --> 00:55:40,520
What are you doing? Grandma wants to know.

736
00:55:40,520 --> 00:55:43,842
I'm watching Dad try to make up with Mom.

737
00:55:55,505 --> 00:55:56,795
So?

738
00:56:00,805 --> 00:56:03,824
Are the stars the same now
as they were back then?

739
00:56:06,260 --> 00:56:07,598
They're not the same.

740
00:56:08,330 --> 00:56:09,860
Then...

741
00:56:09,860 --> 00:56:12,348
which ones are more beautiful?

742
00:56:14,520 --> 00:56:16,895
Probably the ones back then.

743
00:56:23,902 --> 00:56:26,990
I'm sleepy.
I probably used up too much energy today.

744
00:56:26,990 --> 00:56:28,809
I'll go to sleep now, Ran.

745
00:56:31,184 --> 00:56:33,750
Don't. You stay here.

746
00:56:33,750 --> 00:56:38,150
You look like you have a lot
to say to Uncle Yai.

747
00:56:42,709 --> 00:56:44,470
Wait, Ran.

748
00:56:44,470 --> 00:56:46,817
Is there something you'd
like to talk to me about?

749
00:56:48,790 --> 00:56:49,966
No.

750
00:56:51,722 --> 00:56:54,137
Then stay here and stargaze with me.

751
00:56:55,560 --> 00:56:56,668
I'm glad.

752
00:56:57,720 --> 00:57:00,160
I'm so happy I got to be with you.

753
00:57:02,896 --> 00:57:06,606
Because I don't know
if we'll talk like this again tomorrow.

754
00:57:09,300 --> 00:57:11,450
If I die tomorrow...

755
00:57:11,450 --> 00:57:13,560
Don't talk about dying.

756
00:57:13,560 --> 00:57:15,262
I don't want you to die.

757
00:57:16,540 --> 00:57:18,949
Then say what you want to say to me.

758
00:57:20,323 --> 00:57:21,996
I want to hear it.

759
00:57:23,000 --> 00:57:24,731
Say you love me.

760
00:57:27,410 --> 00:57:30,597
You only have to say you still love me.

761
00:57:33,496 --> 00:57:34,949
Can you do that?

762
00:57:38,761 --> 00:57:39,809
Yes,

763
00:57:41,700 --> 00:57:43,395
I love you, Yai.

764
00:58:02,976 --> 00:58:06,576
<i>- ♪ I won't let anything bring you harm ♪
- ♪ I won't let anything bring you harm ♪</i>

765
00:58:07,900 --> 00:58:09,705
Lek is so extra.

766
00:58:11,200 --> 00:58:13,190
Let me say this.

767
00:58:13,190 --> 00:58:15,506
I won't let our daughter be a singer.

768
00:58:16,400 --> 00:58:17,500
Why?

769
00:58:17,500 --> 00:58:20,050
Well, she's still young.

770
00:58:20,050 --> 00:58:22,190
She should focus on her studies first.

771
00:58:22,190 --> 00:58:24,910
Being famous at a
young age isn't easy to handle.

772
00:58:25,640 --> 00:58:28,025
You're even more serious than I am.

773
00:58:29,876 --> 00:58:32,796
<i>- ♪ Baby, I love you ♪
- ♪ Baby, I love you ♪</i>

774
00:58:34,280 --> 00:58:37,770
<i>- ♪ Baby, I love you ♪
- ♪ Baby, I love you ♪</i>

775
00:58:46,390 --> 00:58:50,420
I just learned that...
my brother has a cute side to him.

776
00:58:50,420 --> 00:58:51,658
Lek,

777
00:58:52,760 --> 00:58:56,087
you've always been my third wheel
ever since we were kids.

778
00:58:57,554 --> 00:58:59,376
My niece is done singing.

779
00:59:04,270 --> 00:59:07,400
She's quite talented. She sang perfectly.

780
00:59:07,400 --> 00:59:10,652
She had a great teacher. Thank you, Lek.

781
00:59:36,380 --> 00:59:38,480
When we were younger,

782
00:59:38,480 --> 00:59:41,514
we dreamed of a beautiful future.

783
00:59:44,136 --> 00:59:47,306
But in reality,
it's nothing like we dreamed, right?

784
00:59:48,380 --> 00:59:51,460
But we can choose to keep living happily.

785
00:59:52,110 --> 00:59:53,580
Do you agree with me?

786
00:59:55,898 --> 00:59:57,214
I agree.

787
00:59:58,520 --> 01:00:04,049
My happiness is seeing my daughter
and brother graduate

788
01:00:04,049 --> 01:00:05,690
and get good jobs,

789
01:00:06,790 --> 01:00:08,190
seeing Mom healthy,

790
01:00:09,780 --> 01:00:11,623
and seeing you succeed.

791
01:00:14,900 --> 01:00:18,430
What about your life? Have you ever thought...

792
01:00:19,870 --> 01:00:21,944
about your own future again?

793
01:00:26,880 --> 01:00:28,643
I'll answer that for you.

794
01:00:31,682 --> 01:00:33,966
Your future is...

795
01:00:34,555 --> 01:00:36,728
you'll be my wife,

796
01:00:38,887 --> 01:00:40,762
a great mother,

797
01:00:42,380 --> 01:00:45,050
and I'll make you happy.

798
01:00:45,766 --> 01:00:47,117
No more struggling

799
01:00:48,214 --> 01:00:50,081
or sorrow.

800
01:00:55,243 --> 01:00:58,623
And I'll make Dao
the happiest kid in the world.

801
01:01:05,940 --> 01:01:09,490
Say something too, Ran. I want to hear it.

802
01:01:09,490 --> 01:01:11,481
I was the only one talking.

803
01:01:16,400 --> 01:01:17,768
I...

804
01:01:19,688 --> 01:01:20,996
love you

805
01:01:22,240 --> 01:01:23,560
so much.

806
01:01:24,540 --> 01:01:26,124
I love you all this time.

807
01:01:27,130 --> 01:01:29,224
I love you the most, Yai.

808
01:01:29,830 --> 01:01:31,466
Can you say it again?

809
01:01:33,340 --> 01:01:34,854
I love you.

810
01:01:35,620 --> 01:01:36,620
Again.

811
01:01:38,694 --> 01:01:40,410
I love you, Yai.

812
01:01:53,794 --> 01:01:55,233
I love you too, Ran.

813
01:01:56,380 --> 01:01:58,143
I've always loved you.

814
01:02:13,880 --> 01:02:17,650
Hey, Yai, why can't I join in?

815
01:02:17,650 --> 01:02:19,900
Don't butt in. It's none of your business.

816
01:02:19,900 --> 01:02:21,410
Do your work.

817
01:02:21,410 --> 01:02:22,650
<i>I see.</i>

818
01:02:22,650 --> 01:02:26,508
So this was your plan to make me work today.

819
01:02:30,727 --> 01:02:32,116
Yai?

820
01:02:48,060 --> 01:02:50,395
What is the surprise?

821
01:02:50,395 --> 01:02:51,759
You'll find out soon.

822
01:02:58,210 --> 01:02:59,578
Yai,

823
01:03:00,253 --> 01:03:02,029
You can do it.

824
01:03:16,220 --> 01:03:18,174
Will you marry me?

825
01:03:19,150 --> 01:03:20,500
Yai...

826
01:03:21,453 --> 01:03:24,010
Can you give me another chance?

827
01:03:25,660 --> 01:03:28,710
Let me make things right between us,

828
01:03:28,710 --> 01:03:31,268
just like I promised you back then.

829
01:03:32,240 --> 01:03:33,971
Even though it's...

830
01:03:36,017 --> 01:03:38,033
ten years late,

831
01:03:38,764 --> 01:03:40,479
but it's still not too late.

832
01:03:42,385 --> 01:03:43,667
Will you marry me?

833
01:03:51,255 --> 01:03:52,141
Yes.

834
01:03:53,063 --> 01:03:55,009
I'll marry you.

835
01:04:24,480 --> 01:04:27,817
- Kiss, kiss.
- Kiss, kiss.

836
01:04:40,156 --> 01:04:43,080
<i>- I love you.
- I love you too.</i>

837
01:05:20,867 --> 01:05:22,940
- Daddy.
- Yes?

838
01:05:22,940 --> 01:05:24,760
- Mommy?
- Yes?

839
01:05:24,760 --> 01:05:26,815
Kiss your daughter's cheeks.

840
01:05:38,375 --> 01:05:40,789
What a rascal.

841
01:05:46,320 --> 01:05:48,107
Do you like it here?

842
01:05:49,580 --> 01:05:51,400
I do.

843
01:05:51,400 --> 01:05:53,580
Because I was born here.

844
01:05:58,387 --> 01:06:00,107
I love this place so much.

845
01:06:02,300 --> 01:06:04,115
I love this place so much too.

846
01:06:05,260 --> 01:06:07,091
Because here, I have you

847
01:06:07,700 --> 01:06:09,201
and your mother.
